  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $4$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column.",
